# The agent needs its own credential: the Agent SDK does not read the Claude
# Code desktop app's keychain entry. Set ONE of the following.

# Option A — bill your Claude subscription. Run `claude setup-token` and paste
# the token it prints here.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Option B — bill the Anthropic API account.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Let the agent drive a tab in your own Chrome. Off by default.
# JOBSEARCH_BROWSER=1

# Split Pilot, the extension in extension/. It holds the two panes, keeps
# links out of new tabs, AND is the Playwright target, so this is the only
# browser extension you need.
#
# Chrome derives an unpacked extension's id from the path it was loaded from,
# so yours differs from anyone else's. Copy it from the extension's card in
# chrome://extensions. Setting it makes npm install point the pinned
# Playwright at your extension; leaving it unset points Playwright at
# Microsoft's Playwright Extension instead, which you would then have to
# install.
# JOBSEARCH_SPLIT_EXTENSION_ID=

# The token Playwright presents when it connects. The app hands it to the
# extension, so you do not have to; it is here because the server passes it to
# Playwright. Approving the first connection in the browser also works.
# PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_EXTENSION_TOKEN=

# Optional overrides.
# JOBSEARCH_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# JOBSEARCH_DATA_DIR=~/.jobsearch
# PORT=5179

# Browser behaviour when you watch in a Chrome split view.
# A tab group cannot sit in a split pane, so grouping is off by default.
# JOBSEARCH_BROWSER_TAB_GROUP=1      # put controlled tabs back in a group
# JOBSEARCH_BROWSER_BACKGROUND=1     # stop Playwright focusing the tab each step
# JOBSEARCH_BROWSER_PROFILE=Default  # pin the Chrome profile to connect to

# Scoring postings is a judgement about one document, so it runs on a cheaper
# model than the chat. Raise it to claude-sonnet-5-5 if the reasoning is thin.
# JOBSEARCH_ASSESS_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# JOBSEARCH_ASSESS_CONCURRENCY=4
